  "description": "MOZJIY crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C192 H132 Dy12 N36 Na1 O44 P6,C3 H7 N1 O1,2(C2 H3 N1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.899-4.560 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.90-114.46°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C199H146Dy12N39NaO46P6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
